# Files rsconnect should not ship to a Shiny host.
#
# .Rprofile is the important one: it does source("renv/activate.R"), but
# rsconnect excludes renv/ from the bundle, so the host is left with an
# .Rprofile pointing at a file that is not there and R fails to start with
# "cannot open file 'renv/activate.R'". The host installs the packages listed
# in renv.lock itself, so it has no use for renv's activation machinery.
.Rprofile
renv

# Development and packaging files the running app has no use for. app.R calls
# pkgload::load_all(), which needs DESCRIPTION, NAMESPACE, R/ and inst/ -- so
# those must stay.
.github
.Rbuildignore
.dockerignore
.rscignore
Dockerfile
data-raw
man
tests
rsconnect
